	db	254,1,0,'INTERVIEW: Big Bad Bertha',255
	db	250,2,0,8,11,104
	db	22,17,65
	db	253,65
	db	'ZX-Woot is in a lesser-known area of Soho to interview Big Bad Bertha from Renegade. We arranged to meet '
	db	'at her establishment "Big Bertha',39,'s Brothel & Retrocomputing Emporium.',232
	db	'ZXW: Hello. You must be Bertha, I',39,'m here for the interview.',232
	db	'BBB: Hya. That',39,'s fine, let me check - Ok - Natasha is free for an "interview", '
	db	'as you call it. The rates are $50 for a happy handshake, $100 for Horatio, $375 ',253,0
	db	'for a walk in the woods and $500 for a trip to the junkyard. But no funny business - '
	db	'if you try any rough stuff with my girls I',39,'ll rip your nuts off and shove them down y-',232
	db	'ZXW: NO! No. I',39,'m here about the matter we discussed on the phone. The interview? '
	db	'About your time on Renegade?',232
	db	'BBB: Oh I see! Sorry I thought you were one of the punters. Let',39,'s go to the back office. Go ahead.',232
	db	'ZXW: Tell us about your time working on Renegade.'
	db	255
	;
page_bertha1:
	db	248
	db	251
	db	254,1,0,'INTERVIEW: Bertha (page 2)',255
	db	22,17,0
	db	'BBB: It wasn',39,'t a great job. They put me in an unflattering vest top and kegs and the only direction I '
	db	'had was "just run at him and let him kick you in the head". I had to stand by and watch all my girls get '
	db	'punched in the chuff, and then get pummelled myself. I wouldn',39,'t stand for it now. I can',39,'t even say the money was good.',232
	db	'ZXW: Were you disappointed not to appear in any of the Renegade sequels?',232
	db	'BBB: Oh but I did. I was one of the dinosaurs. The only good news about that was that nobody could see my face. '
	db	'The on-set atmosphere wasn',39,'t very good, as it was obvious that the whole project was going to be a turkey. '
	db	'Everyone tried their best, the costumes were good, the sets more than serviceable, but there was no escaping '
	db	'the fact that it was a bloody time travelling beat em up! Which bellend came up with that idea?! If it was the '
	db	'6th in the franchise it',39,'d be more understandable, but the third? Nah.'
	db	255
	;
page_bertha2:
	db	248
	db	251
	db	254,1,0,'INTERVIEW: Bertha (page 3)',255
	db	22,17,0
	db	'ZXW: What did you do after the Renegades?',232
	db	'BBB: I spent several years as a nightclub bouncer, then started a management company for other bouncers, general heavies, '
	db	'and hitmen',59,' and then I realised the real money was in prostitution. So I did an NVQ in boudoir management and advanced '
	db	'Madaming and set up my own spot in Soho.',232
	db	'ZXW: And you',39,'re still in the trade I see.',232
	db	'BBB: Well, being a Madame is recession-proof, so I',39,'ll never stop doing that, but I',39,'ve diversified. '
	db	'I noticed how popular the whole "retro" thing has become, and people always want sex, so I decided to put the two together. '
	db	'We have a games room with ZX-Spectrums, Amstrads and even a C64 for the real perverts. It',39,'s a middle-aged '
	db	'man',39,'s paradise. In fact the computer room is probably more popular than the girls. Some of the punters only come in for the gaming, '
	db	'and some of them are interested in the girls, but "they just want to talk"... about retrogaming. So I',39,'ve had to make sure '
	db	'all my girls are au-fait with everything from early 80s games to modern homebrew, with a smattering of hardware knowledge. '
	db	255
	;
page_bertha3:
