	db	250,2,0,9,10,40
	db	251
	db	254,1,0,'REVIEW: SINCLAIR A-BIKE',255
	db	253,73
	db	22,19,73
	db	'In a small village near Bremen, in 1846, Gunter Bikemayker stood forlorn in his workshop. Clutching his redundancy notice and divorce papers, '
	db	'he looked at his tools and felt an intense, burning hatred for mankind. It was at this point that Gunter resolved to make the worst bicycle '
	db	'in the world, to punish humanity for wronging him so badly. After a few weeks',39,' work, Gunter stood back and examined his creation.',253,0,' He called '
	db	'it the "HasseBike". It had square wheels, a spike for a seat, chocolate handlebars, no gears (or drivetrain), and as it moved a mechanical hand '
	db	'poked the rider repeatedly in the kidneys. Gunter succeeded - it was undoubtedly the worst bike the world had ever seen, and it held this record '
	db	'until the 12th July 2006, when the Sinclair A-Bike was unleashed upon the world.',232
	db	'Now, none of that is true, but it hopefully makes a mildly amusing introduction to my experience of the A-bike. I bought mine in 2018, while online '
	db	'and at the thin end of a bottle of wine.',232
	db	255
	;
page_ABike1:
	db	243
	dw	ABikeSCR
	db	250,2,0,9,10,96+128
	db	251
	db	254,1,0,'REVIEW: SINCLAIR A-BIKE (2)',255
	db	253,73
	db	22,19,73
	db	'At best I hoped for a fun curio I could ride about, and maybe use for short commutes during busy rail '
	db	'journeys. When the bike arrived, I was impressed by its style and compactness. Folding and unfolding the A-Bike is not intuitive, but once '
	db	'you learn the trick it is quick and easy. So far so good - then I tried riding it. The tiny 6" wheels are made of rock-solid rubber, '
	db	'so everything ',253,0,'except a perfectly planar surface is unbearable. And that',39,'s the good bit over with, because this bike is PROPERLY unsafe. '
	db	'It',39,'s a good job you can',39,'t go very fast, because the tiniest pothole will have you upended on the floor. The frame is so small, '
	db	'that anyone of average height and above will look ridiculous on it, and struggle to peddle with bent legs.',232
	db	'However, I was determined to stick with it, because I paid good money for it, and the gearing and brakes do deserve some credit for being well-made. '
	db	'So I took it on a train journey.',232
	db	255
	;
page_ABike2:
	db	243
	dw	ABikeSCR
	db	250,2,0,9,10,222
	db	251
	db	254,1,0,'REVIEW: SINCLAIR A-BIKE (3)',255
	db	253,73
	db	22,19,73
	db	'I walked a short way to the station with the bike already folded. This is where the A-Bike impresses - it',39,'s light '
	db	'to carry and easy to stow on even the busiest train. It was when I alighted to ride it the problems started. I felt frankly ridiculous on '
	db	'this slow, rattly bike. I don',39,'t know how much it really stood out, but I was so embarrassed that I was glad it was getting dark. Then the '
	db	253,0,'lightest drizzle started, and I found the A-Bike',39,'s latest flaw. The slick wheels and tiny frame do not want to balance or go forward when '
	db	'the ground is slightly wet - it wants to go sideways and slam you on your hip. After the second time this happened, I lay on the ground with '
	db	'the drizzle licking my face, and wondered how engineering',39,'s answer to SQIJ could ever be deemed fit for sale, and why did I love Sinclair '
	db	'products so much? I had no answer, other than to stand up, fold-up the A-Bike and walk to my destination with it - after all - this bike carries great...',232
	db	255
	;
