tip0:	db	'Instead of buying Spectrums listed on ebay as "not tested but it should work", keep a broken '
	db	'48K in your attic, and post it to yourself.',232,'A.N. Other, Dorset.',255
tip1:	db	'Keep flies out of your Spectrum',39,'s circuitry by storing raw meat on top of it, rather than inside.',232,'M. Trellis, N Wales.',255
tip2a:	db	'PERVERTS. Try resting your knackers on a hot 128K heatsink for a thrill.',232,'F. Boff, email.',255
tip2b:	db	'PERVERTS. Putting your knackers on a hot 128K heatsink is not as sexually gratifying as you might think.',232,'F. Boff, email.',255
tip3:	db	'Get the warm fuzzy nostalgia of RAMpack wobble by jiggling a screwdriver in the USB port of your PC.',232,'L. Spoons, Bellend.',255
tip4:	db	'GAMERS. Tweet a picture of yourself loading a game, then you don',39,'t need to play it.',232,'A.D.H. Dee, email.',255
tip5:	db	'Recreate the EM radiation of your old CRT telly by sellotaping some Strontium-90 on top of your laptop.',232,'J. Smith, Saffron Walden.',255
tip6:	db	'Fool your neighbour into thinking you have a ZX-Spectrum by buying a dial-up modem.',232,'J. Apester, Dundee.',255
tip7:	db	'CODERS. Save time by not putting anything after a REM statement - BASIC ignores it anyway.',232,'B. Pape, Muckle Flugga.',255
tip8:	db	'CODERS. Stop hackers by making your game so appalling that nobody can be bothered.',232,'Power House Software.',255
tip9:	db	'DAVID CAMERON. If you break your mate',39,'s 48K by plugging the joystick interface in when switched ON, don',39,'t run away.',232,'T. May, Ibiza..',255
tip10:	db	'NOUVEAU-RICHE MINERS. Avoid having a large clearing-up task in the morning by asking party-going revellers to tidy up as they go along.',232,'Maria, Surbiton.',255
tip11:	db	'Save a miniscule fraction of your time by just typing J rather than LOAD before pressing <SYMBOL SHIFT> and P, twice, then <ENTER>, then waiting five minutes to play a '
	db	'game.',232,'Uncle Clive, Cambridge.',255
tip12:	db	'ADVENTURERS. Prevent over-enthusiastic Dwarves from starting to sing about gold by not letting them sit down.',232,'B.Baggins, The Shire.',255
tip13:	db	'SOFTWARE COMPANIES. Stamp out piracy COMPLETELY by making games that are so crap the tape they',39,'re on has more value as a blank tape.',232
	db	'Cascade Software, address not supplied.',255
tip15:	db	'Learn Piano Easily and develop incredible finger/brain independence by alternating between CURSOR/PROTEK and SINCLAIR INTERFACE 2 control methods each game.',232
	db	'T.Stamper, Ashby-de-la-zouche',255
tip16:	db	'ENTREPRENEURS. For maximum profit, bolt on a "datacorder" to an existing product and pretend it',39,'s a new one.',232,'A.Sugar, address supplied.',255
tip17:	db	'VLOGGERS. Circumvent controversy by never ever making any jokes about old intellectual property with disputed ownership.',232,'Horace (Mrs). Ski Lodge Lane, The Alps.',255
tip18:	db	'Prove the superiority of your machine over that of C64 owners',39,' by showing off your rubber-massaged fingertips next to their calloused '
	db	39,'real key',39,' worn ones.',232
	db	'R.Dickinson (genius).',255
tip19:	db	'See the ending of games by turning the cassette over, and loading them backwards.',232,'R.T.L Ererre, France.',255
tip20:	db	'SOFTWARE Houses. Trick children into buying your awful games by putting in-game screenshots from a system '
	db	'with superior graphics on the cassette cover with a microscopic disclaimer explaining that "Screenshots may be from different versions"'
